# Copy to `app/.env` and fill in. `app/.env` is gitignored; this file is not.
#
# ── ★ THIS APP NEEDS NO BROWSER CREDENTIAL, AND THEREFORE NO VARIABLE HERE ──────
#
# The site map's basemap is **keyless**: MapLibre GL JS paints tiles served by
# OpenFreeMap, which serves anyone who asks — no token, no account, no allowed-origin
# list. There is therefore nothing to fill in, and nothing whose absence can blank the
# panel. (Before this swap the map used Mapbox with a `pk.` token kept here; that token
# turned out not to be entitled to the Styles/Tiles APIs, so removing the requirement
# was the fix rather than re-scoping the credential.)
#
# Everything else this page shows — the two mileages, the drawn road route, the
# turn-by-turn steps — is stored in this app's own database
# (`vendor_site_route` / `geo_origin`) and was never fetched from a map API in the
# browser. See the header comment of `src/components/VendorSiteMap.tsx`.
#
# ── IF YOU EVER SWAP THE BASEMAP ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The style URL lives on one line in `src/components/VendorSiteMap.tsx`. A substitute
# needs to be a *complete* style document — one that names its own `sources`, `glyphs`
# and `sprite` — because this component supplies only a container, a centre and an
# attribution control that reads the credit out of the style itself.
# `<host>/styles/<name>` is the shape to look for.
#
# ── THE MAPBOX TOKEN IS STILL NEEDED, BUT ONLY BY THE SERVER ────────────────────
#
# `server/src/scripts/geocode-vendor-sites.ts` (geocoding, the driving Matrix and
# Directions) runs in Node, where Mapbox's URL restrictions do not apply — it sends no
# `Referer`, which is the header those restrictions are enforced against. That token
# belongs in the **root** `.env` as `MAPBOX_API_KEY`, never in a file Vite inlines into
# the client bundle.
#
# ★ Vite's `envDir` is this folder, so a variable put here is compiled into the shipped
#   JavaScript; the root `.env` — which holds ORACLE_PASSWORD, the Turso token and the
#   database URLs — is never read by the bundler at all. Do not set `envDir: ..` to
#   reach one variable: it would hand the build every one of them the moment any gains
#   a `VITE_` prefix.
